Z||000000||kornholio||10-06-1999||06:45 PM||||I have no idea how old my fuel filter is. If I replace it, will I get better gas mileage? Right now, I get about 250 km (155 miles) out of a full tank of gas.  I have an auto 86 SE with a 10.3 gallon tank.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Dave85||10-06-1999||07:24 PM||||Man, sorry to hear about your mileage!! That really SUCKS. I would replace that filter anyway. Maybe it'll help, maybe not but at least you'll know that it's been done.||||reg||1
Z||000002||RZURCTN||10-06-1999||07:51 PM||||Your Fiero should be getting much better mileage!  I would go with a major tune up and timing check.  Mileage should be 27mpg in town to 42mpg on the highway.  That all depends on how heavy your foot is!!  Happy tunin'!<BR>Ted||||reg||1
Z||000003||kornholio||10-06-1999||08:05 PM||||Since I bought this car, I have done the following:  change the plugs, wires, air filter, distributor cap and rotor. What else should I do besides replace the fuel filter?||||reg||1
