Z||000009||Greg Piet||10-07-1999||10:12 AM||||I must admit I dont get anyhting like 40 mpg<BR>in a 2.8  4sp (with 100K miles)if i do a tank on the highway i get about 27-30.<BR>Most of the time I am doing really short trips in city traffic, where I get about 20 mpg (and I am heavy on the gas when those lights turns green).<BR>As an aside, I only get to use about 8.5 gallons of petrol per tank. (I've been thinking about adding a fuel cell, but havent looked into it,so if anyone has some keen info on this,post a new topic on it)<BR>||||reg||2
Z||000010||Dave85||10-07-1999||10:28 AM||||If your fuel tank is like mine, you can add another 3 galons after it clicks off. When I first got the car I was filling to the next even amount past the click. It was only taking about 6 gal. I just thought my gauge was wacked.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Dave85||10-07-1999||10:34 AM||||Kornholio, check your miles divided by galons used. That will give you your MPG. You may find it's not that bad.I have v6 and my last tank I got 21.5 mpg. That's with a week of my foot being glued to he floor board!!!  I have gotten as high as 50 mpg on the road.||||reg||1
